"requests":1},"T5e":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1347.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":271.44444444444446,"requests":1},"T6":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1707.625,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":129.375,"requests":1},"T9":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1707.625,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":129.375,"requests":1},"necessity":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1707.625,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":129.375,"requests":1},"prerequisite-consistency":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":9698.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":120.0,"requests":1},"project.portability":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":1707.625,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":129.375,"requests":1},"project.symbol-reference-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":0.0,"cache_write_tokens":0.0,"input_tokens":205151.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":5145.0,"requests":7}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an AC that exercises the mapper-level fail-closed directly (e.g. `_map_local_to_jira_fields`/`_map_local_to_dc_fields` raise on an undecided type absent from `type_map`), or state that the up-front gate makes the mapper branch unreachable and the branch is purely defensive.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach: 'Type resolution + fail-closed live in TWO upstream places — the up-front gate and the mapper.'","Finding 4: '(4) `outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields` (:101) resolves issuetype via `type_map` (replacing coerce :143), fail-closed; (5) DC `_map_local_to_dc_fields` (coerce :86) same.'","No AC names a mapper-level fail-closed; `test_fail_closed_fires_before_mutation_loop` exercises `compute_outbound_mutations` (the gate)."],"finding":"The mapper-level fail-closed branch (Finding 4 items 4 & 5: `outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields` and DC `_map_local_to_dc_fields` resolve issuetype via `type_map` 'fail-closed') is a described deliverable in TWO places ('Type resolution + fail-closed live in TWO upstream places — the up-front gate and the mapper') but only the up-front gate has a covering AC (`test_fail_closed_fires_before_mutation_loop`). The mapper-level fail-closed has no dedicated covering criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fddead8281bf03f91","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Finding 4 (items 4/5) vs Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"neb39c7e0d5d05c89","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A regression removes the mapper's fail-closed branch but keeps the gate; the second defensive layer silently degrades with all ACs still green."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add `test_mapper_fails_closed_on_undecided_type` covering both field mappers, or annotate the mapper fail-closed as a defensive assertion covered indirectly by the gate.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the inbound census/Scope to apply_inbound_events._inbound_create_write_create_event (:76/:111): prefer a rebar-type: label (via recover_type_label) over the raw _JIRA_TYPE_MAP derivation, mirroring the recover_status_label call at :156, and add apply_inbound_events.py to Scope.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan census lists only: 'NEW inbound_fields.recover_type_label (mirror recover_status_label :152) + _LOCAL_TYPE_VOCAB from get_args(TicketType); wired at :311-313, label-over-raw :326.'","apply_inbound_events.py:76 `ticket_type = _JIRA_TYPE_MAP.get(issuetype, \"task\")` then apply_inbound_events.py:111 `\"ticket_type\": ticket_type` in the CREATE event — a Jira->local type derivation NOT covered by the census.","The sibling status path apply_inbound_events.py:156 `local_status: str | None = recover_status_label(raw_labels)` proves this module was intentionally kept in parity with inbound_fields for the status annotation — the type analogue is missing."],"finding":"The inbound recovery inventory for the new rebar-type: round-trip omits apply_inbound_events.py, a second Jira->local type-derivation site. inbound_fields.recover_status_label has TWO structural consumers (inbound_fields._map_jira_to_local_fields AND apply_inbound_events._inbound_create_write_status_event:156), and the parallel raw-type derivation apply_inbound_events._inbound_create_write_create_event:76 (`ticket_type = _JIRA_TYPE_MAP.get(issuetype, 'task')`, written into the CREATE event at :111) mirrors inbound_fields' _JIRA_TO_LOCAL_TYPE path. The plan's census names only inbound_fields (:311-313, :326), so the bootstrap-create import path never prefers a rebar-type: label over the raw issuetype.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f87af26b1bc6b9fc2","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Surface-parity census — 'Inbound: NEW inbound_fields.recover_type_label (mirror recover_status_label :152) ... wired at :311-313, label-over-raw :326'","norm_id":"ndc8b11315aadf48c","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A lossy-collapsed local type imported through the bootstrap-create path (apply_inbound_events._inbound_create_write_create_event) lands at the raw _JIRA_TYPE_MAP result (e.g. Story->story) instead of the rebar-type: label's intended local type, silently breaking the round-trip for freshly imported/bound issues while the bound-ticket differ path (inbound_fields) round-trips correctly.","apply_inbound_events.py is absent from the plan's Scope file list, so the create-path type recovery is never patched or tested."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In apply_inbound_events._inbound_create_write_create_event, resolve ticket_type as `recover_type_label(raw_labels) or _JIRA_TYPE_MAP.get(issuetype, \"task\")` (raw_labels are already gathered at :82), exactly as the STATUS phase prefers recover_status_label(raw_labels); list apply_inbound_events.py in Scope and add a create-path round-trip AC.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"n